555
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,900
[Carefully waiting for the one
who's on the same wavelength.]

556
00:21:13,666 --> 00:21:15,266
I feel better after we talked.

557
00:21:15,266 --> 00:21:16,133
Isn't that a good thing?

558
00:21:16,133 --> 00:21:17,233
I feel better about her now.

559
00:21:17,266 --> 00:21:19,066
Not sure how she feels about me.

560
00:21:23,533 --> 00:21:31,033
[Is someone falling asleep tonight
with unspoken thoughts?]

561
00:21:35,933 --> 00:21:38,233
Twelve days... too short, huh?

562
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:40,900
Does it feel like time is slowing down?

563
00:21:43,933 --> 00:21:45,433
I have no idea what day it is

564
00:21:45,466 --> 00:21:46,533
or even the date.

565
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:48,533
All I know is

566
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:49,933
it's day nine.

567
00:21:51,533 --> 00:21:57,266
[Day9 Today's Affection Moon Phase:
Waxing Gibbous]

568
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:06,833
[Antioxidant Activity Monitoring]

569
00:22:07,033 --> 00:22:10,100
[Tip: Eat more fruits and vegetables.]

570
00:22:11,633 --> 00:22:13,666
[Switching to Running Mode]

571
00:22:21,333 --> 00:22:23,600
[Starting a New Day with Morning Jog]

572
00:22:25,300 --> 00:22:26,700
I just think it's too short.

573
00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:28,966
Our time on the island is too short.

574
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:31,666
How long would feel right to you?

575
00:22:31,666 --> 00:22:32,333
Twenty days?

576
00:22:33,133 --> 00:22:34,466
I wanna stay on this island forever.

577
00:22:34,633 --> 00:22:35,633
[I wanna stay on this island forever.]

578
00:22:38,933 --> 00:22:39,766
I can't.

579
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:42,266
I'd die of awkwardness.

580
00:22:45,200 --> 00:22:45,900
No, I meant

581
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:49,733
I wish everything
we've felt and experienced here

582
00:22:49,733 --> 00:22:51,733
could last.

583
00:22:53,300 --> 00:22:54,000
Yeah.

584
00:22:55,100 --> 00:22:57,800
After graduation,
we barely get that chance

585
00:22:57,833 --> 00:23:00,100
to interact with people
without all the labels attached.

586
00:23:02,033 --> 00:23:03,700
The world gets more complicated.

587
00:23:03,700 --> 00:23:05,033
That's the era we're in.

588
00:23:05,066 --> 00:23:08,366
Social media, information everywhere...

589
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:11,866
People keep getting partial information...

590
00:23:11,866 --> 00:23:12,466
Getting information

591
00:23:12,466 --> 00:23:14,700
they're not supposed to be seeing now.

592
00:23:14,700 --> 00:23:15,800
And then form opinions

593
00:23:15,833 --> 00:23:18,366
that they think are 'mature'.

594
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:21,133
So I think the younger the generation,

595
00:23:21,133 --> 00:23:22,400
the more realistic they'll be.

596
00:23:22,433 --> 00:23:22,833
Yeah.

597
00:23:22,833 --> 00:23:25,533
And they're maturing earlier.

598
00:23:25,533 --> 00:23:26,600
Yes.

599
00:23:26,633 --> 00:23:29,066
The island is the most comfortable place.

600
00:23:36,400 --> 00:23:37,900
So when Xiaxia comes back,

601
00:23:37,900 --> 00:23:39,900
how am I supposed to talk to her?

602
00:23:40,333 --> 00:23:42,666
I don't know. Up to you.

603
00:23:42,700 --> 00:23:44,366
Qianyu, any advice?

604
00:23:44,400 --> 00:23:45,733
I am curious,

605
00:23:45,733 --> 00:23:48,033
on a scale of 1 to 100,

606
00:23:48,066 --> 00:23:49,666
how would you rate

607
00:23:49,666 --> 00:23:52,133
your feelings for her?

608
00:23:52,533 --> 00:23:55,000
Looks-wise, she's totally my type.

609
00:23:55,033 --> 00:23:57,633
But I barely got a chance to talk to her.

610
00:23:57,633 --> 00:23:59,866
Barely spent any time with her.

611
00:24:01,333 --> 00:24:03,166
Every time I wanted to talk to her,

612
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:04,933
she was gone.

613
00:24:04,933 --> 00:24:07,166
I almost camped outside her door,

614
00:24:07,200 --> 00:24:08,300
pitched a tent or something.

615
00:24:08,300 --> 00:24:10,500
But I can't tell who she likes.

616
00:24:10,500 --> 00:24:13,500
You're acting like
there are only two options, A or B.

617
00:24:13,500 --> 00:24:16,166
[Subtle]
But what if she's actually got a C?

618
00:24:18,266 --> 00:24:19,366
C...

619
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:21,866
And C doesn't have to be a person.

620
00:24:21,866 --> 00:24:23,766
You get what I mean?

621
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:26,200
[Maybe neither of them is in her options.]

622
00:24:29,900 --> 00:24:31,000
Yeah, so I...

623
00:24:31,033 --> 00:24:33,633
I don't know what to talk about.

624
00:24:33,633 --> 00:24:35,266
[Hinting Failed]
Did you have fun?

625
00:24:35,266 --> 00:24:36,300
What did you guys do?

626
00:24:36,300 --> 00:24:38,033
Where did you go? Was it fun?

627
00:24:38,066 --> 00:24:39,000
I spent two survival points.

628
00:24:39,033 --> 00:24:39,700
My only two.

629
00:24:39,700 --> 00:24:40,533
You know what?

630
00:24:40,533 --> 00:24:41,866
He had two left, I had three.

631
00:24:41,900 --> 00:24:43,000
We both bought the card.

632
00:24:43,033 --> 00:24:43,966
[Bankrupting Himself for the Sneak Peek]
Now I only have one survival point left.

633
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:44,900
[Bankrupting Himself for the Sneak Peek]
He's got none.

634
00:24:45,733 --> 00:24:47,766
Pan and Huihui

635
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:48,666
are really a good match.

636
00:24:48,900 --> 00:24:49,900
[So Shippable]

637
00:24:49,900 --> 00:24:51,200
I saw their pictures there.

638
00:24:51,233 --> 00:24:52,933
[Too Sweet]
I was laughing like crazy.

639
00:24:52,933 --> 00:24:54,200
They are so sweet.

640
00:24:54,233 --> 00:24:55,566
I kinda miss him though.

641
00:24:56,933 --> 00:25:00,033
[Waking Up Early to Prepare Breakfast]

642
00:25:06,733 --> 00:25:07,600
[Pan's Exclusive]

643
00:25:07,633 --> 00:25:09,233
[Pan's Exclusive]
These are "scattered eggs".

644
00:25:09,400 --> 00:25:11,333
[Loving Breakfast]

645
00:25:12,466 --> 00:25:13,333
Room service.

646
00:25:13,400 --> 00:25:14,333
[Butler Pan at Your Service]

647
00:25:16,266 --> 00:25:17,400
You finished?

648
00:25:17,433 --> 00:25:18,233
Come have breakfast.

649
00:25:18,733 --> 00:25:20,233
That's a lot.

650
00:25:20,266 --> 00:25:21,466
Let me make you a sandwich.

651
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:21,933
[Pan will be taking care of you today.]

652
00:25:21,933 --> 00:25:22,966
[Pan will be taking care of you today.]
What fillings do you want?

653
00:25:23,033 --> 00:25:24,033
[Pan will be taking care of you today.]
This?

654
00:25:24,100 --> 00:25:25,400
Eggs.

655
00:25:25,666 --> 00:25:27,400
But it's a bit bland.

656
00:25:27,433 --> 00:25:29,100
These are "scattered eggs".

657
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:30,033
[Pan's Exclusive Scattered Egg]

658
00:25:30,066 --> 00:25:30,866
Okay?

659
00:25:30,866 --> 00:25:31,166
Okay.

660
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:34,200
My dad came up with that name.

661
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:37,000
Why are you so energetic in the morning?

662
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:38,533
You didn't sleep well?

663
00:25:38,533 --> 00:25:40,666
It's not that.

664
00:25:40,700 --> 00:25:41,966
How is it, boss?

665
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:43,300
Enough.

666
00:25:43,933 --> 00:25:45,400
Enough.

667
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:50,400
[Pan's Exclusive Sandwich]

668
00:25:50,500 --> 00:25:51,900
Kinda ugly.

669
00:25:52,466 --> 00:25:53,733
It's okay.

670
00:25:56,033 --> 00:25:58,366
[Let me try it.]

671
00:25:58,433 --> 00:25:59,100
[How was it?]

672
00:25:59,100 --> 00:26:00,600
[How was it?]
I didn't taste anything in my first bite.

673
00:26:00,633 --> 00:26:01,866
Only some bread.

674
00:26:04,933 --> 00:26:05,866
It's so sweet.

675
00:26:05,900 --> 00:26:06,800
[The bread is so sweet.]

676
00:26:11,033 --> 00:26:12,366
Let me sit down.

677
00:26:14,866 --> 00:26:16,266
How's my sandwich looking?

678
00:26:18,066 --> 00:26:21,533
[Mm-hm]

679
00:26:21,533 --> 00:26:23,533
[Encrypted Conversation]

680
00:26:23,533 --> 00:26:25,400
[Mm? Mm. Mm!]

681
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:27,000
Did you get what I said?

682
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:28,400
Did you get what I said?

683
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:36,666
The egg is the most delicious.

684
00:26:36,666 --> 00:26:38,866
I gotta eat more.

685
00:26:39,733 --> 00:26:41,433
Then we're heading back to the island.

686
00:26:46,833 --> 00:26:48,233
We're going back to the island.

687
00:26:48,233 --> 00:26:49,666
I kinda miss it though.

688
00:26:49,666 --> 00:26:51,200
Miss your friends?

689
00:26:51,233 --> 00:26:51,900
Yeah.

690
00:27:04,933 --> 00:27:06,433
Fifteen minutes.

691
00:27:06,466 --> 00:27:07,666
[15 Minutes Left]

692
00:27:07,733 --> 00:27:09,166
Legs are sore, hands are sore.

693
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:11,900
[One Playful Punch]
My head's spinning, and my back hurts.

694
00:27:11,900 --> 00:27:12,366
[One Playful Punch]

695
00:27:12,400 --> 00:27:13,000
[Two Playful Punch]

696
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:14,633
[Massaging Her Leg]
Why would the legs be sore?

697
00:27:14,633 --> 00:27:15,733
[Massaging Her Leg]

698
00:27:16,100 --> 00:27:16,900
Massage.

699
00:27:17,866 --> 00:27:19,133
We walked too much yesterday.

700
00:27:19,133 --> 00:27:20,233
And my left leg is fine.

701
00:27:20,266 --> 00:27:21,366
It's only my right leg.

702
00:27:25,600 --> 00:27:27,633
That means...

703
00:27:27,633 --> 00:27:29,633
I walked with my right leg
doing all the work.

704
00:27:31,800 --> 00:27:34,933
It could be
when we were 'Catching Moon in Water',

705
00:27:35,666 --> 00:27:38,166
my right leg was in front.

706
00:27:40,133 --> 00:27:42,333
On that second part of your rap that day,

707
00:27:42,333 --> 00:27:43,666
did you do that character's voice?

708
00:27:43,700 --> 00:27:44,366
Xiong Er's.

709
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:45,466
I can do it again.

710
00:27:45,466 --> 00:27:46,000
Say

711
00:27:46,033 --> 00:27:48,266
[Looking Forward]
'Xiong Da, I want honey.'

712
00:27:48,633 --> 00:27:50,033
Xiong Da.

713
00:27:50,033 --> 00:27:51,300
Xiong Da.

714
00:27:51,300 --> 00:27:53,333
I want honey.

715
00:27:54,733 --> 00:27:56,133
Xiong Da.

716
00:27:56,133 --> 00:27:59,066
Qiang is cutting trees again!

717
00:27:59,800 --> 00:28:01,333
You're killing me.

718
00:28:02,866 --> 00:28:04,333
I knew you were imitating him

719
00:28:04,333 --> 00:28:05,800
when you did that.

720
00:28:06,500 --> 00:28:07,800
Only you noticed.

721
00:28:07,833 --> 00:28:08,733
Mm-hm.

722
00:28:08,733 --> 00:28:09,666
Mm-hm.

723
00:28:09,700 --> 00:28:11,366
'Mm-hm' means 'noted'.

724
00:28:11,400 --> 00:28:12,800
And there's a 'Mm, yeah'.

725
00:28:12,800 --> 00:28:14,600
'Mm, yeah' means you're annoyed.

726
00:28:14,600 --> 00:28:16,033
Mm.

727
00:28:16,033 --> 00:28:17,633
'Mm' means you're furious.

728
00:28:17,633 --> 00:28:18,700
Fine, then.

729
00:28:18,700 --> 00:28:19,966
'Fine, then' means speechless.

730
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:21,200
Oh.

731
00:28:21,533 --> 00:28:22,566
'Oh' means I'm screwed.

732
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:23,533
['Oh' = I'm screwed.]

733
00:28:23,666 --> 00:28:24,733
[Level 10 Master of Huihui Language]

734
00:28:24,733 --> 00:28:26,133
[Pleased]

735
00:28:26,933 --> 00:28:28,166
Its ears are really big.

736
00:28:29,100 --> 00:28:30,033
My ears are big too.

737
00:28:32,033 --> 00:28:33,300
[Squeezing Earlobes]
My earlobes are big.

738
00:28:33,300 --> 00:28:34,566
[Squeezing Earlobes]
Let me see.

739
00:28:34,600 --> 00:28:35,233
[Squeezing Earlobes]

740
00:28:35,700 --> 00:28:37,700
I used to love squeezing earlobes.

741
00:28:37,700 --> 00:28:38,933
Did you squeeze your own?

742
00:28:38,933 --> 00:28:39,666
Like this?

743
00:28:40,833 --> 00:28:42,166
Feels really nice.

744
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:43,866
I like it.

745
00:28:43,866 --> 00:28:46,166
Sometimes I even think

746
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:48,033
this chunk of meat would taste great.

747
00:28:49,233 --> 00:28:50,866
Sometimes I touched it in class,
and I'd get hungry and think,

748
00:28:51,866 --> 00:28:53,966
"What's for lunch?"

749
00:29:04,333 --> 00:29:05,633
[Apologizing in a Low Voice]
Sorry.

750
00:29:07,466 --> 00:29:08,166
Pinch me back.

751
00:29:08,200 --> 00:29:09,033
[You can pinch me back.]

752
00:29:11,900 --> 00:29:13,600
You pinched so hard!

753
00:29:15,066 --> 00:29:16,300
I mean...

754
00:29:21,500 --> 00:29:24,166
That sharp, tiny force.

755
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:25,400
The first pinch

756
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:27,466
[Wide Awake]
scared me to death.

757
00:29:31,900 --> 00:29:33,433
[Numb]

758
00:29:33,466 --> 00:29:35,066
Now I'm used to it.

759
00:29:39,400 --> 00:29:40,833
We're here.

760
00:29:40,833 --> 00:29:42,300
Right?

761
00:30:03,600 --> 00:30:04,433
Time to eat!

762
00:30:04,466 --> 00:30:05,400
[Picking Up Pu for Dinner]

763
00:30:05,866 --> 00:30:07,000
What's wrong?

764
00:30:07,033 --> 00:30:07,933
Just woke up.

765
00:30:10,333 --> 00:30:11,566
Close the door.

766
00:30:12,866 --> 00:30:15,533
[Holding Onto Him]

767
00:30:15,666 --> 00:30:16,200
Time to eat.

768
00:30:16,233 --> 00:30:17,166
You're wearing a silk scarf.

769
00:30:17,200 --> 00:30:18,666
I just noticed.

770
00:30:18,933 --> 00:30:20,066
My styling trick.

771
00:30:20,100 --> 00:30:21,033
Hi.

772
00:30:21,066 --> 00:30:22,000
Hi.

773
00:30:22,033 --> 00:30:23,566
We're coming.

774
00:30:25,800 --> 00:30:27,033
What are you doing?

775
00:30:27,033 --> 00:30:27,700
Get you some meat.

776
00:30:27,700 --> 00:30:29,166
Don't you like that dish?

777
00:30:29,233 --> 00:30:30,933
[Getting Food to Pu]

778
00:30:33,733 --> 00:30:35,400
Tomato scrambled eggs.

779
00:30:35,433 --> 00:30:36,733
Tomato scrambled eggs.

780
00:30:37,433 --> 00:30:38,700
More eggs, please.

781
00:30:39,700 --> 00:30:40,800
Thanks.

782
00:30:42,733 --> 00:30:43,566
Thank you.

783
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:44,700
[A Full Bowl]

784
00:30:44,700 --> 00:30:45,366
[A Full Bowl]
You're sweet.

785
00:30:45,400 --> 00:30:46,033
[A Full Bowl]

786
00:30:51,133 --> 00:30:52,200
Delicious. Eat some.

787
00:30:52,866 --> 00:30:54,100
Sit.

788
00:30:54,433 --> 00:30:55,466
Anyone want water?

789
00:30:55,466 --> 00:30:56,400
Thanks.

790
00:30:57,066 --> 00:30:57,966
Anyone else?

791
00:30:58,000 --> 00:30:59,200
Me too.

792
00:30:59,200 --> 00:30:59,733
All gone.

793
00:30:59,733 --> 00:31:00,766
He's a porter now.

794
00:31:01,200 --> 00:31:01,866
Thank you.

795
00:31:02,333 --> 00:31:05,133
[Porter]

796
00:31:05,600 --> 00:31:06,900
Your eyedrops.

797
00:31:06,900 --> 00:31:08,533
[Giving You the Best]
Best eyedrops I've ever used.

798
00:31:09,433 --> 00:31:10,100
Here you go.

799
00:31:10,400 --> 00:31:12,066
[Thanks for the eyedrops.]

800
00:31:14,500 --> 00:31:16,433
[Huihui & Pan are back.]

801
00:31:16,833 --> 00:31:17,733
They're back!

802
00:31:21,866 --> 00:31:23,066
I missed you.

803
00:31:23,066 --> 00:31:24,500
You missed me?

804
00:31:25,033 --> 00:31:26,466
[Carrying a Lot of Things]

805
00:31:26,700 --> 00:31:28,300
Are those our gifts?

806
00:31:28,300 --> 00:31:28,733
Of course.

807
00:31:28,733 --> 00:31:30,266
Yeah, this is for you.

808
00:31:30,333 --> 00:31:32,400
[Gifts!]

809
00:31:32,733 --> 00:31:33,600
Was it fun?

810
00:31:33,633 --> 00:31:34,533
Did you like it?

811
00:31:34,533 --> 00:31:35,433
Yeah.

812
00:31:35,500 --> 00:31:36,933
[Envious]

813
00:31:37,066 --> 00:31:38,966
[Giving Out Sweet Gifts]
We bought gifts for everyone.

814
00:31:39,000 --> 00:31:40,233
Tao,

815
00:31:40,233 --> 00:31:41,300
does it look like you?

816
00:31:42,100 --> 00:31:43,500
[Happy]
Yes.

817
00:31:43,700 --> 00:31:44,933
[Curious]
What is it? Let me see.

818
00:31:46,266 --> 00:31:47,900
Good.

819
00:31:47,900 --> 00:31:49,766
Autumn, I picked one for you.

820
00:31:49,800 --> 00:31:52,333
A little doll that looks just like you.

821
00:31:52,333 --> 00:31:54,333
Really? Now I'm curious.

822
00:31:54,333 --> 00:31:55,200
Huihui chose it for you.

823
00:31:55,233 --> 00:31:56,133
Said it looks like you.

824
00:31:56,133 --> 00:31:58,333
Thank you.

825
00:31:58,900 --> 00:32:01,133
It even matches Tao's one quite well.

826
00:32:01,500 --> 00:32:02,533
Oh, no... now we match?

827
00:32:03,133 --> 00:32:04,666
How did I end up matching with you?

828
00:32:05,100 --> 00:32:06,233
[Hmph]

829
00:32:06,266 --> 00:32:07,300
This is for Jerry.

830
00:32:07,300 --> 00:32:08,900
Thank you.

831
00:32:08,900 --> 00:32:09,600
I can't wait any longer.

832
00:32:09,633 --> 00:32:10,733
Let me take a look.

833
00:32:10,733 --> 00:32:12,133
